Based on the council's outbuilding guidance, a garden shed under 2.5 metres high, set behind the front wall of the house and covering less than half the garden, does not usually need a planning application.

Two things could change that:

- **Conservation areas and listed buildings** have different rules, so a shed there may need an application even if it's small.
- **Constraints on your property** such as a tree preservation order could also affect things.

If you give me your full address, I can check whether any of these constraints apply. If you already have a planning application reference, I can look that up as well. Please note this is general guidance, not a formal planning opinion. If you're unsure, it's worth confirming with the planning desk before you build.
